course: dictionary
lesson: 6006
title: Words that tell how something is done
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Mechanically is an adverb. It tells you how someone does an action. Its first meaning is "by a machine or using machinery", and its second is "without thinking, like a robot".
explain: In «Mechanically the Rat repacked the basket», the clue is "like a machine, without thinking". The Rat goes through the action without deciding each move. Then he goes on to choose «a stout stick», which shows he is thinking again, so the first action was automatic.
explain: Use the swap test. Put "without thinking" in place of mechanically: "the Rat repacked the basket without thinking". It still makes sense, so you have the right meaning. A third meaning, "mechanically minded", describes a person who is good at understanding how machines work.
fact: Mechanically means by a machine or using machinery.
fact: Mechanically can also mean doing something without thinking, like a robot.
fact: Mechanically minded means good at understanding how machines work.
fact: In design and technology, a gate may be opened mechanically, by a motor or a lever rather than by hand.
fact: In a story, a character who answers mechanically may be numb, bored or sad.
exercise: «Mechanically the Rat repacked the basket.» What does mechanically suggest here? | * Doing it without thinking, like a robot | Doing it while singing | Doing it very carefully and slowly
exercise: A factory gate is opened mechanically. What does this mean? | * It is opened by a machine or motor | A person opens it gently with their hand | It opens by itself, like magic
exercise: Priya says she is mechanically minded. What does this mean? | She is always late for school | * She is good at understanding how machines work | She likes painting pictures
test: Ben answers his teacher's questions mechanically, in a flat voice with no smile. What does this suggest? | * He is numb or bored | He is thinking very hard about a machine | He is excited about the lesson | He is asleep under his desk
test: Which phrase means "good with machines"? | Mechanically cold | Mechanically noisy | * Mechanically minded | Mechanically late
exam: In «Mechanically the Rat repacked the basket», what does the word tell us about how the Rat acted? | Carefully, after long thought | * Without thinking, like a machine | Angrily, slamming things down | Sadly, with tears in his eyes
